    "body": "## Description\n\nAdd a `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml` file to customize the issue creation page — for example, directing users to Discord for general questions instead of opening an issue.\n\n## Steps to Complete\n\n1. Create `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml`.\n2. Configure it to:\n   - Disable blank issues (force users to pick a template).\n   - Add a contact link pointing to the Discord server.\n   - Optionally add a second link to the GitHub Discussions page, if enabled.\n3. Commit with `chore: add issue template config`.\n4. Open a pull request.\n\n## Example structure\n\nReference the GitHub documentation for the exact YAML keys.\n\n## Learning Outcomes\n\n- Understanding GitHub's issue template configuration.\n- Improving contributor experience before they even open an issue.\n\n## Helpful Resources\n\n- [GitHub Docs: Configuring issue templates](https://docs.github.com/en/communities/using-templates-to-encourage-useful-issues-and-pull-requests/configuring-issue-templates-for-your-repository)\n",
